Chapter: Ed25519CallersSmallOrderTest
  cites Verify chapter CdxBinary
  cites Trust chapter Handshake
  cites Trust chapter TrustLattice
  cites Foreword chapter Ed25519

 SignatureSlippage part B. The two callers whose message is their input
 verbatim, under a key the input itself supplies: a CDX header's stored
 content hash under its own header key, and a handshake nonce under the
 peer's claimed key. A = R = 32 zero bytes and S = 0 (red's
 ed25519-small-order vectors); a message of byte b then 31 zeros puts h mod 4
 at 0, 1, 2, 3 for b = 1, 0, 8, 4, and a verifier with no small-order check
 accepts b = 4.

Section: Helpers
  show-bool : Boolean -> Text
  show-bool (b) = if b then "True" else "False"

  so-zeros : Integer -> List Integer
  so-zeros (n) = if n == 0 then [] else [0] & so-zeros (n - 1)

  so-msg : Integer -> List Integer
  so-msg (b) = [b] & so-zeros 31

  so-header : Integer -> List Integer
  so-header (b) = so-zeros 8 & so-msg b & so-zeros 32 & so-zeros 64

  so-row : Integer, Integer -> Text
  so-row (cls) (b) =
    let cdx = cdx-verify-signature (so-header b)
    in let hs = hs-receive-prove (so-msg b) (so-zeros 32) (so-zeros 64) lattice-empty
    in "h mod 4 = " & show cls & ": cdx-signature accepted=" & show-bool cdx
      & " handshake failed=" & show-bool (hs-is-failed (hs.state))

Section: Body
  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (so-row 0 1)
    print-line-uni (so-row 1 0)
    print-line-uni (so-row 2 8)
    print-line-uni (so-row 3 4)
  end
